From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 10:07:59 +0200
Subject: net: lantiq: dma: remove the channel interface nothing drives

The packet DMA driver offers a per-channel configuration interface:
packet drop policy, packet size, byte offset, traffic class, software
poll interval, peripheral-to-peripheral pairing, the data buffer
allocator behind it, and a port teardown.

The network device that drives this datapath uses seven entry points of
this driver - reset a channel, free and configure its descriptors, turn
it on and off, and mask and unmask its interrupt - and no others. Every
function listed above was called from the peripheral-to-peripheral relay
bring-up, which is gone, or from the ioctl surface of the deleted suite,
or from nowhere at all. The port teardown never had a caller at all:
nothing in this driver ever unwinds a port once it is open.

Remove them, and the width test that only the buffer allocator asked.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

